        "schema_version": "text/plain.numbered-nl.v1",
        "content": "1 This state machine model represents the train's basic braking device, which serves as the final execution unit for train braking operations. \n2 When the basic braking device receives a brake signal, it transitions from the initial state to the braking state. If the signal transmission fails, it proceeds to the operational state. Once the signal feedback is sent, it returns to the initial state. \n3 After entering the braking state, the system transitions to the brake caliper clamping state.",
